  "headline": "Propofol is not on FDA's current shortage list as of 2026-10-21; the earlier shortage first posted 2020-04-10 is resolved",
  "headline_cites": ["D17"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's records show propofol is not on the current shortage list as of 2026-10-21; the earlier shortage first posted on 2020-04-10 has been resolved.",
      "cites": ["D17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the 2020 shortage episode, FDA inspected the Pfizer Healthcare India plant (FEI 3008316085) and classified it OAI on 2019-09-06, with the classification letter dated 2020-05-25, 45 days after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E15", "D16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the same plant on 2020-03-25, 16 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Fresenius Kabi Uppsala plant (FEI 3002631703) and Fresenius Kabi Austria plant (FEI 3003708554) have only VAI classifications in FDA's inspection history.",
      "cites": ["E19", "E20", "E21", "E22", "E23", "E24", "E25", "E27", "E28", "E29", "E30", "E31", "E32", "E33"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 343 vials of 10 mg/mL 20 mL propofol (21.7 days on hand) and can spare 18 vials while retaining a two-week supply.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale Lakeside holds 10 vials of the same presentation (5 days on hand) and would reach 14 days after receiving the transfer.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The recommended action is to transfer 18 vials of 10 mg/mL 20 mL propofol from Corvale General to Corvale Lakeside, which requires a pharmacy director transfer request.",
      "cites": ["D18"]
    }
  ]
}
